ROCKNIX ABL (https://github.com/ROCKNIX/abl), GPL-2.0, (c) ROCKNIX contributors.
Steps and scripts follow ROCKNIX and Armada (https://github.com/armada-os/armada).

Flashing the wrong ABL can brick the device. Match the SoC carefully:

  SM8550 - Retroid Pocket 6, Retroid Pocket Nova, AYN Thor
  SM8650 - KONKR Pocket FIT (8 Gen 3)

1. Copy the rocknix_abl folder from this card to the root of Android
   internal storage.

2. In Android settings, use "Run script as root": browse to your SoC's
   folder (e.g. rocknix_abl/SM8550) and run backup_abl.sh. It writes
   abl_a.img and abl_b.img into that folder.

3. Copy abl_a.img and abl_b.img to your PC and keep them.
   restore_backup_abl.sh puts them back if you ever want the stock ABL.

4. Run flash_abl.sh the same way.

5. Reboot holding VOL- to open the ABL menu (VOL-/+ to move, POWER to pick):
     - Set the device model
     - Set boot mode to Linux
     - Start
   Android still boots from the same menu.
